/*
  KB2040 multi-board USB composite: CDC-ACM (Serial) + CDC-NCM (Ethernet) + WebSocket Web UI + OTA

  Target : Adafruit KB2040 (FQBN rp2040:rp2040:adafruit_kb2040:flash=8388608_4194304)
           8 MB flash = 4 MB sketch + 4 MB LittleFS (slot config + OTA staging).
  Core   : earlephilhower/arduino-pico, default "Pico SDK" USB stack (Serial and
           NCMEthernetlwIP enumerate together; 1200-baud touch reset stays active).

  Addressing (slot stored in LittleFS /slot.txt, 0 = default/unassigned):
    slot 0    : 192.168.7.1/24    mDNS kb2040.local
    slot 1..4 : 192.168.7N.1/24   mDNS kb2040-N.local (+ alias kb2040.local)
    The built-in DHCP server leases <net>.2.. to the host, with no router and no DNS option.

  HTTP (port 80):
    GET  /                       Web UI
    GET  /ws                     WebSocket (RFC 6455): telemetry push + JSON commands
    GET  /api/state              telemetry JSON
    POST /api/led?state=on|off|toggle   /api/interval?ms=N   /api/slot?slot=N
    POST /api/identify   /api/reboot   /api/cmd (JSON command body)
    GET  /api/firmware.bin       the running image, read straight from XIP flash
    POST /api/update             raw .bin body (optional X-CRC32 header) -> LittleFS -> PicoOTA

  Serial (newline-delimited): JSON commands ({"cmd":...}) or LED:ON|LED:OFF|LED:TOGGLE|STATE|
    IDENTIFY|INTERVAL:<ms>|SLOT:<n>|REBOOT|BOOTSEL|OTA:START:<size>[:<crc32hex>]

  Physical BOOT button held 3 s: forget the slot (back to 192.168.7.1) and reboot.
*/

